  "qualitative_review": "Across seeds 42, 123 and 2026, the beta4 variants have broadly similar digit readability and softness. FH128 and F8 do not show a convincing visual generation advantage over F4/FH64. F4/FH32 has the lowest measured negative ELBO (106.6972) and grayscale MSE (0.021322) within the beta4 group. F2/FH64 is close (negative ELBO 106.8673), with similar-looking samples and the shortest recorded training time. These are useful candidates, not a statistically established generation ranking: each configuration has one training seed. The three inference seeds do not substitute for independent training repeats. Beta4 remains the qualitative generation choice for its generally simpler, more coherent shapes, with softer edges and worse reconstruction/ordinary ELBO than the beta1 reference. No further training was authorized or launched after the five specified runs.",
